## FAQs

### What AV equipment is needed for a conference?

A typical conference needs PA sound reinforcement, a projector or LED display for slides, and wired, wireless or gooseneck microphones for the podium and panel discussions. Larger conferences with breakout rooms need a second, smaller setup for each parallel session.

### How much does audio visual rental for a conference cost?

Pricing depends on the package: our full catalog, from the Basic MICE Pack for a small executive session up to the MICE Pack for a full conference, is listed with exact euro pricing on our [packages page](/packages/). All rates are ex VAT, with 21 percent Spanish VAT added at checkout, and every price includes delivery, setup and teardown.

### How is a conference AV setup different from a corporate event or press conference?

A corporate event is usually a single room with one setup. A press conference is built around one speaker area and a podium mic. A conference is the more demanding case: a plenary session plus one or more breakout rooms running in parallel, each needing its own sound and screen. See [How This Differs from a Corporate Event or Press Conference](#how-this-differs-from-a-corporate-event-or-press-conference) above.

### Can you run AV for a plenary session and breakout rooms on the same day?

Yes. The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) covers the plenary with a technician on site, and the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) covers a smaller breakout or executive session. Book both together for a multi-room conference day.

### How far in advance should I book AV for a conference?

Book as early as you can once your date and room layout are confirmed, especially if your conference needs both a plenary and breakout rooms covered on the same day. Demand on the Costa del Sol peaks during the spring and autumn conference season.

